.TH TRANSIP-DNS 1 "October 2026" "transip-rest" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
transip-dns \- manage DNS records at TransIP from the command line
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B transip-dns
.RB [ --global-key ]
.BI --username\~ USER
.BI --key-file\~ KEYFILE
.I command
.RI [ args ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B transip-dns
authenticates to the TransIP API v6 using an RSA key pair and manages
DNS records (A, AAAA, CNAME, MX, NS, TXT, SRV, SSHFP, TLSA, CAA,
NAPTR) for domains in that TransIP account.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI list\~ DOMAIN
List all DNS entries for
.IR DOMAIN .
.TP
.BI add\~ DOMAIN\~NAME\~TYPE\~CONTENT\~ "[\-\-ttl SECONDS]"
Add a DNS entry. Default TTL is 86400 seconds.
.TP
.BI delete\~ DOMAIN\~NAME\~TYPE\~CONTENT\~ "[\-\-ttl SECONDS]"
Delete a DNS entry. The
.I name
,
.IR type ,
.I content
and
.I ttl
must all match the live record exactly, or TransIP will not find a
match to delete.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --username\~ USER
TransIP account login.
.TP
.BI --key-file\~ KEYFILE
Path to the RSA private key (PEM) registered for this account.
.TP
.B --global-key
Request a token that works from any IP, instead of one limited to
whitelisted IPs.
.SH SEE ALSO
.UR https://api.transip.nl/rest/docs.html
TransIP REST API documentation
.UE
